# Source is text, always. Without this git classifies a file by sniffing it, and a
# single stray control byte — a NUL written as a raw byte instead of \0, say — makes
# git call the whole file binary: no diff, no blame, and grep walks past it. That
# happened silently to four files before it was noticed. `diff` is the attribute that
# forces the text treatment (`text` only governs line-ending normalisation, which is
# already a no-op here — every tracked file is LF).
*.ts    text diff
*.tsx   text diff
*.js    text diff
*.jsx   text diff
*.json  text diff
*.jsonc text diff
*.md    text diff
*.sh    text diff
*.py    text diff
*.css   text diff
*.html  text diff
*.sql   text diff
*.yml   text diff
*.yaml  text diff

# Assets that really are binary.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff2 binary
*.avif  binary
*.webp  binary
